From b471395e87521c3330541ffe5889d88e253ff33d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(post): per-post script suites on recorded edge-case
 streams

Every shipped post script (assets/posts/*.cps) gets a suite in
crates/post/tests (script_<stem>.rs) that runs the post binary on nine
recorded .cnc streams - arcs in each plane and a helix, a full circle
(as generated, and as one hand-written 360-degree record), a peck cycle
with a retract change, a tool change with a spindle direction change, a
rotary index and a tilted move (on tilthead.mch), a probing cycle, an
empty section, very small and very large coordinates - and compares the
program or the named refusal with a golden beside the suites. No app,
no toolpath generation in the suites.

Staleness guards: recorded_streams (post) rebuilds the six cl-built
streams through post::dump; app's recorded_post_streams rebuilds the
probe and drill streams from motion; the hand-written stream parses and
round-trips. Post bugs the goldens showed are filed (#994-#998) and the
wrong outputs are listed as known bugs, not baked into goldens.

Slice 1; moving the ten app tests is left for slice 2.

Refs #926

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
